  "title": "CMake: If building with Qt 6, require at least Qt 6.2",
  "description": "6.2 is still pretty old, but that's what's available with Ubuntu\n22.04 (Jammy) (and PPAs for earlier Ubuntu releases.) Even that\nwill allow getting rid of a lot of QT_VERSION_CHECKs once Qt 5\nis completely removed.\n\nFix #17378 (because CMake won't allow compiling on macOS with a\nversion that would produce that warning message.)",
